These now clear storage that the HTTP endpoints also write to, so routing through the `grpc*Service` objects reads as gRPC-only. Calling `storage` directly is accurate and lets the forwarding `getRequests()` and `clearRequests()` methods go away from the three gRPC classes (same for `/get-traces`, `/get-metrics`, and `/get-logs` on lines 107, 116, and 125).

```suggestion
